There is no user profile API in this working directory (it holds only Claude config files), and file writes were not approved, so nothing is on disk and the code below has not been run. It is a standalone TypeScript cache layer you can drop in; I guessed the language.

It is an in-memory, per-process cache keyed by user ID, with a TTL (60s default), LRU eviction (10,000 entries default) and explicit invalidation.

```ts
// profileCache.ts
export interface ProfileCacheOptions {
  ttlMs?: number;
  maxEntries?: number;
}

interface Entry<T> {
  value: T;
  expiresAt: number;
}

